{"name":"Pineapple Juice","hex":"#f8e87b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pineapple juice","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The juice of pineapples; used as a beverage or in cocktails, e.g. piña colada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pineapple_juice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pineapple juice","blocks":[{"text":"Pineapple juice is a juice made from pressing the natural liquid out from the pulp of the pineapple. Numerous pineapple varieties may be used to manufacture commercial pineapple juice, the most common of which are Smooth Cayenne, Red Spanish, Queen, and Abacaxi. In manufacturing, pineapple juice is typically canned."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Batido_de_pi%C3%B1a.jpg/330px-Batido_de_pi%C3%B1a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pineapple_juice","wikidata":"Q3190226"},{"title":"Pineapple","blocks":[{"text":"The pineapple is a tropical plant with an edible fruit; it is the most economically significant plant in the family Bromeliaceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/%E0%B4%95%E0%B5%88%E0%B4%A4%E0%B4%9A%E0%B5%8D%E0%B4%9A%E0%B4%95%E0%B5%8D%E0%B4%95.jpg/330px-%E0%B4%95%E0%B5%88%E0%B4%A4%E0%B4%9A%E0%B5%8D%E0%B4%9A%E0%B4%95%E0%B5%8D%E0%B4%95.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pineapple","wikidata":"Q1493"},{"title":"Juice","blocks":[{"text":"Juice is a drink made from the extraction or pressing of the natural liquid contained in fruit and vegetables. It can also refer to liquids that are flavored with concentrate or other biological food sources like meat or seafood, such as clam juice. Juice is commonly consumed as a beverage or used as an ingredient or flavoring in foods or other beverages, such as smoothies. Juice emerged as a popular beverage choice after the development of pasteurization methods enabled its preservation without using fermentation. The largest fruit juice consumers are New Zealand and Colombia. Fruit juice consumption on average increases with a country's income level."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Orange_juice_1.jpg/330px-Orange_juice_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juice","wikidata":"Q8492"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Pina_Colada_Top.JPG/500px-Pina_Colada_Top.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Pina_Colada_Top.JPG/1280px-Pina_Colada_Top.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Pina_Colada_Top.JPG/500px-Pina_Colada_Top.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Piña colada with garnish","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APina_Colada_Top.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Pinus_coulteri_MHNT_Cone.jpg/500px-Pinus_coulteri_MHNT_Cone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Pinus_coulteri_MHNT_Cone.jpg/1280px-Pinus_coulteri_MHNT_Cone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Pinus_coulteri_MHNT_Cone.jpg/500px-Pinus_coulteri_MHNT_Cone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APinus_coulteri_MHNT_Cone.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Pineapple_and_cross_section.jpg/500px-Pineapple_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna